      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems wrong to set the USB enable bits before we\u0027ve been told we have something plugged in.  We should probably be hanging out in safe state until the task sets us to something on plug-in.  I think a lot of the datasheet is geared towards approaches where USB_EN is only turned on when something is plugged in, based on the power-on sequence and workflow (in the datasheet, as opposed to the programming guide).\n\nIt does look like the TC should set the muxes before we apply Vbus, which should hopefully make the chip happy.",
